# Large generated data artifacts -- deterministically regeneratable from the committed
# scripts/configs/seeds; not committed to keep the repo reproducible-but-light. To be
# hosted externally (e.g. Hugging Face Datasets / GitHub Release assets) and linked from
# the relevant experiment's reports/run_metadata instead of being stored in git.
# (Activation shards themselves are already covered by the *.safetensors rule above.)
experiments/activation_extraction_qwen3_1_7b/metadata/prompt_token_metadata.jsonl
experiments/duplicate_language_embedding/embeddings/prompt_embeddings.npy
experiments/duplicate_language_embedding/annotations/language_script_annotations.jsonl

# Milestone 5 (SAE capacity comparison): never commit trained SAE weights/checkpoints
# or residual-stream activation tensors -- only findings, configs, and evaluation
# outputs are tracked. Checkpoints (*.pt) are already covered by the global *.pt rule
# above; these directory-level rules are belt-and-suspenders against any non-.pt binary
# landing in the same places, and explicitly exclude scratch/debug-run byproducts.
experiments/sae_capacity_comparison/checkpoints/
experiments/sae_capacity_comparison/checkpoints_pilot/
experiments/sae_capacity_comparison/models/
experiments/sae_capacity_comparison/**/_aborted_full_run/
experiments/sae_capacity_comparison/**/_scratch_timing_tests/
experiments/sae_capacity_comparison/**/_legacy_overwritten_no_seed_suffix/
# Exception: the frozen preprocessing mu vector is tiny (~9KB, 2048 floats) and is an
# essential reproducibility artifact (every SAE's input transform depends on it) --
# unlike model weights, it is small, deterministic, and needed to reproduce results.
!experiments/sae_capacity_comparison/preprocessing/mu_vector.pt